{
  "id": "garden",
  "title": "Grandma's Greenhouse",
  "story_for_agents": "Level 3 of the grandma story. Grandma has moved out; you and her ginger cat go room by room taking back one memory of you and her. Her little glass greenhouse against the house is where you grew things together every summer: a bamboo cane in the empty raised bed carries five ribbons at rising heights (your height each summer), the cork board shows you planting seeds at four, watering at six, the giant pumpkin at seven, and one photo is missing. The door clicks shut behind you; the key hangs on a hook up under the eaves, far too high, above the raised bed whose painted marker shows a sunflower. The bed sits in the shade of a canvas blind pulled down under the roof. Two threads, either order: (1) tip the upturned pot by the door to find the tap's red handle, fit it, the tap fills the watering can in the tub; water the wilted plant on the bench and as it perks up its leaves lift off the crank hanging under the bench edge. (2) Tip over the little yellow welly to find the shears, snip the twine round grandma's seed tin: inside, a sunflower seed packet on top of the missing photo. Plant the seed in the bed, water it, and wind the blind up with the crank: sunlight floods the bed and the sunflower shoots up to the roof, unfolds and bursts open; its happy shake knocks the key off the hook into the soil. Pin the photo in the empty spot (the memory: you at nine touching the giant sunflower), take the key, open the door to the garden. No words: the story is in the photos, the ribbons on the cane, the crayon drawing on the glass, the shade line on the bed and the light.",
  "coords": "Blender metres, Z up: +Y north (glass garden door), -Y south (whitewashed house wall with the kitchen window, tap and photo board), +X east (raised bed, key on the eaves hook), -X west (potting bench, the blind winder on the post). Camera at (0, 0, 1.30). A mesh belongs to the first visible object that lists it, so the pickups come before the things they sit in or on (crank before the plant, photo before the tin, key before the hook). fx.js moves ownership when a prop changes place (the handle onto the tap, the crank into the winder, the photo onto the board).",
  "camera": { "eye": [0, 0, 1.3], "startYaw": 0, "startPitch": -4, "fov": 78, "back": 0.55 },
  "hints": 3,
